{"id": "EUVD-2026-103010", "enisaUuid": "e73ccf4f-65ca-34d0-b282-23964ec12641", "description": "AipexBase through commit 690adb9 contains a sql injection vulnerability that allows attackers to inject SQL through the order_by and group_by fields of the /api/data/invoke endpoint. Attackers can supply subqueries or EXTRACTVALUE and UPDATEXML functions that bypass the SqlGuard denylist and row-level security, reading other users' rows and tables.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:40:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:56:23", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/aipexbase-dynamic-data-order-by-group-by-sql-injection", "https://github.com/kuafuai/aipexbase/blob/690adb933e72b1ead911badd52caa6d1f71046cd/backend/src/main/java/com/kuafuai/dynamic/condition/OrderByBuilder.java#L24-L67", "https://github.com/kuafuai/aipexbase/blob/690adb933e72b1ead911badd52caa6d1f71046cd/backend/src/main/java/com/kuafuai/dynamic/condition/GroupByBuilder.java#L22-L33", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/aipexbase-through-commit-690adb9-sql-injection-via-api-data-invoke"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hcjf-66qr-8j38", "CVE-2026-111718"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "fe8e024a-401d-3c2c-a677-d0f142276edb", "product": {"name": "aipexbase", "vendor": {"name": "kuafuai"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264690adb933e72b1ead911badd52caa6d1f71046cd"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f93bd050-26c5-3885-b481-791504e292be", "vendor": {"name": "kuafuai"}}], "isExploited": false}